"{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2139/ssrn.7109939\",\n  \"title\": \"A Comparative Linguistic Model of the Indus Script Based on Proto-Indo-Aryan Geochronology and Archaic Pre-Vedic Orthography\",\n  \"authors\": \"Sagar More\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>This paper presents a comparative linguistic model evaluating the structural and phonetic relationships between the Indus script corpus and early Vedic orthography. Grounded in recent palaeo-hydrological timelines of the Saraswati River basin and late Bronze Age geochronology, the study establishes a contextual framework positioning the Indus Valley Civilization within the formative periods of Proto-Indo-Aryan development. Moving away from arbitrary signmatching, this research introduces a systematic cryptographic decoding methodology based on early Sanskrit grammatical paradigms and morphosyntactic structures. By applying these specific phonological constraints to the standard Indus seal sign distributions, the model evaluates whether the script operates as a logosyllabic system with a core consonantal framework. Preliminary results suggest a high degree of structural consistency when testing Indus graphemic sequences against Vedic Sanskrit phonetic rules, providing a reproducible pathway for analyzing sign-to-sound correspondences in the Indus corpus.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2139/ssrn.7109939\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.7109939\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"posted-content\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Elsevier BV', 'container_title': '', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'posted-content', 'member': '78', 'prefix': '10.2139'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"title\": \"Sanskrit Influence on the Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jeyakumar Ramasami\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2025-12-20T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'International Journal of Science and Research', 'container_title': 'International Journal of Science and Research (IJSR)', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '1329-1334', 'issn': ['2319-7064'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '8810', 'prefix': '10.21275'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.4324/9780203945315-13\",\n  \"title\": \"Sanskrit\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.4324/9780203945315-13\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2007-07-26T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.4324/9780203945315-13\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Routledge', 'container_title': 'The Indo-Aryan Languages', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '128-184', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9780203945315'], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '301', 'prefix': '10.4324'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1017/s0003598x00040461\",\n  \"title\": \"The Indus Script Deciphered?\",\n  \"authors\": \"Gerard Clauson; John Chadwick\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>The Scandinavian Institute of Asian Studies was founded as recently as 1967 with a governing body of distinguished scholars appointed by the four contributing countries. With this, its first publication, it has got off to a flying start. Ever since the first specimens of the Indus script were published nearly 40 years ago, it has constituted a standing challenge to scholars with a bent for cryptography. Several attempts have been made to decipher it, but as Sir Mortimer Wheeler remarked, before the publication of this monograph, in <jats:italic>The Indus civilization</jats:italic> (3rd edition, Cambridge, 1968, p. 107, footnote 2), 'the published attempts to do so are invalid'. This judgement is now due for drastic reconsideration. </jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1017/s0003598x00040461\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1969-09-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1017/s0003598x00040461\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 3,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Cambridge University Press (CUP)', 'container_title': 'Antiquity', 'volume': '43', 'issue': '171', 'page': '200-207', 'issn': ['0003-598X', '1745-1744'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '56', 'prefix': '10.1017'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1163/9789004645738\",\n  \"title\": \"The Nominal Sentence in Sanskrit and Middle Indo-Aryan\",\n  \"authors\": \"A.A. Breunis\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1163/9789004645738\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1990-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1163/9789004645738\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"monograph\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 4,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'BRILL', 'container_title': '', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': ['9789004645738', '9789004091238'], 'crossref_type': 'monograph', 'member': '374', 'prefix': '10.1163'}\"\n}"
